SpinTare repair for llama.cpp, against ggml-org/llama.cpp 3bb63cbcbfb62056c84fe9e521b0f3d756d29c32.

Rotary centring with exact add-back: K is cached as R(p)(k - mu) and every score gets q . R(p) mu back,
computed from the position inside the flash-attention decode kernel (LLAMA_KV_DEBIAS_MU=<mu file>,
LLAMA_KV_DEBIAS_MU_PATH=kqpos); prefill adds R(p) mu to the dequantized keys.
Exemption gate (LLAMA_KV_MU_GATE=1): rows with z = 1 - k.mu / |mu|^2 >= 0.5 are cached uncentred and
flagged (F32 flag per cell and KV head); fused write path GGML_OP_KV_MU_GATE. The code comments call it
the sink gate (SG1 / SG2); the documentation calls it the exemption gate.
With no switch set, every graph follows the upstream path.

Apply: git -C <llama.cpp at 3bb63cb> apply <this file>   (scripts/build_llama_cpp.sh does this)

